  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company has abandoned its legacy zero-emission electric truck operations entirely, merging with Azio AI to become a pure-play AI infrastructure provider. It is now focused on AI data centers, enterprise GPU compute, and digital power solutions, chasing explosive demand in the AI infrastructure market. Early momentum includes deployment of off-grid power at a South Texas site with rights to a large acreage capable of scaling to significant capacity, and a newly signed long-term hosting agreement with an expansion path, signaling initial customer validation in a capital-intensive sector.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership executed a wholesale strategic pivot, closing the Azio AI merger and filing for a corporate name change to Azio AI to reflect the new identity. This bet-the-company move leverages the acquired AI infrastructure platform and site rights to quickly secure an anchor hosting customer, demonstrating an aggressive push from transaction close to contracted revenue. The decision to shed the former struggling vehicle business and redirect all resources toward AI infrastructure marks a complete reorientation of strategy and capital allocation, resetting the company’s trajectory.",
